---
/**
 * Privacy notice. Keep it true to the code: update it (and UPDATED) whenever
 * the site starts collecting something new, e.g. analytics or a new form field.
 */
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Eyebrow from '@/components/Eyebrow.astro';
import { getSite } from '@/lib/site';
import { clean, isEmail } from '@/lib/todo';

/** The date this notice last changed (not the build date). */
const UPDATED = new Date('2026-11-17T00:00:00Z');

const site = await getSite();
const name = [site.firstName, clean(site.surname)].filter(Boolean).join(' ');
const email = isEmail(site.email) ? site.email : '';
// Built here, not in the markup, so line wrapping can't eat the spaces.
const owner =
  `This site belongs to ${name}, ${site.title}, based in ${site.location.city}, ${site.location.country}. ` +
  `I'm responsible for the data described here.` +
  (email ? ' You can reach me at ' : '');
const updated = UPDATED.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
});
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy notice · ${name}`}
  description="What this site collects when you use the contact form, why, how long it's kept and how to have it deleted."
>
  <article aria-labelledby="privacy-title" class="shell section-gap">
    <hgroup>
      <Eyebrow label="Privacy" />
      <h1 id="privacy-title" class="type-page-title mt-3">
        Privacy notice
      </h1>
    </hgroup>
    <p class="type-lead measure mt-5 text-muted">
      The short version: this site has no analytics, no tracking and no cookies. The only personal
      data it collects is what you send through the contact form, and that's used only to reply to
      you.
    </p>
    <p class="type-small mt-4 text-muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="privacy measure mt-12">
      <h2>Who's responsible</h2>
      <p>
        {owner}
        {email && (
          <a class="link" href={`mailto:${email}`}>
            {email}
          </a>
        )}
        {email && '.'}
      </p>

      <h2>What the contact form collects</h2>
      <p>When you send a message, I receive:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name and email address</li>
        <li>the project type and, if you pick one, the budget range</li>
        <li>your message</li>
        <li>your IP address and the time you sent it, so I can spot spam and abuse</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The message arrives as an email in my inbox. It isn't stored in a database or added to a
        mailing list, and it isn't shared with anyone or used to train AI models.
      </p>
      <p>
        To stop spam, the server also counts how many messages each connection sends in an hour. For
        that it keeps your IP address only in scrambled form (a keyed hash), which can't be turned
        back into the address, along with the times you sent messages. Records older than an hour
        are cleared out automatically.
      </p>

      <h2>Why I use it</h2>
      <p>
        Only to read your message and reply to it, and if we go ahead, to discuss and plan the work.
        Under the UK and EU GDPR, the legal basis is taking steps you've asked for before a possible
        contract, and my legitimate interest in answering enquiries and keeping the form free of
        spam.
      </p>

      <h2>How long I keep it</h2>
      <p>
        I keep enquiries for as long as we're in touch about the work, and then for up to two years
        so I have a record of past conversations. If we work together, project emails are kept as
        long as the law requires for business records. You can ask me to delete your messages sooner
        at any time.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
      <p>
        The site and its mailbox are hosted by Hostinger. Like any web host, Hostinger keeps
        standard server logs (IP address, pages requested, browser type and time) for security and
        to keep the service running. I don't use these logs to identify or track visitors.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and storage</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no cookies. If you switch between light and dark mode, your choice is saved
        in your browser's local storage so the site remembers it next time. It stays on your device,
        and you can clear it in your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
      <p>
        Links to GitHub, LinkedIn, certificate issuers and client websites take you to sites with
        their own privacy policies. Nothing from those sites loads on this one.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see the data I hold about you, correct it, have it deleted or object to how
        it's used.
        {email && (
          <>
            {' '}
            Email{' '}
            <a class="link" href={`mailto:${email}`}>
              {email}
            </a>{' '}
            and I'll reply within one month.
          </>
        )}{' '}
        If you're in the UK or EU and unhappy with my answer, you can also complain to your data
        protection authority, such as the ICO in the UK.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this notice changes, for example because the site starts using analytics, the new version
        will be posted here with a new date.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy h2 {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
    font-size: 1.375rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
    font-stretch: 108%;
    font-weight: 650;
  }
  .privacy h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .privacy p,
  .privacy ul {
    margin-top: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .privacy ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    list-style: disc;
  }
  .privacy li + li {
    margin-top: 0.375rem;
  }
  .privacy li::marker {
    color: var(--signal-ink);
  }
</style>
